Make the profile selector logo 5x larger.

Upstream draws the branding mark above "Choose a Profile" at a 64x64 .logo
(profile-selector.css). RozeLynx replaces that slot with a proper illustration,
and at 64px it is too small to read -- the 707x460 landscape scene in
branding/main/no-text.png is centre-cropped into a square, so what survives at
64px is the smallest part of the mark.

320px is 5x the upstream size. The asset is unchanged: this is purely a
consumer-side size, and the ebuild raises the raster embed in
rozelynx_install_vector_slot for about-logo.svg from 192 to 960 so the new size
still has 3x device-pixel headroom rather than upscaling a 192px embed.

Identical in Firefox 155 and 156.

--- a/browser/components/profiles/content/profile-selector.css
+++ b/browser/components/profiles/content/profile-selector.css
@@ -16,8 +16,12 @@
 }

 .logo {
-  width: 64px;
-  height: 64px;
+  /* RozeLynx: upstream's 64px suits a small monochrome mark; this slot holds a
+   * full illustration (see branding/PLACEHOLDERS.md), which is unreadable at
+   * that size. The column is centred with padding: 8%, so growing the logo does
+   * not disturb the layout -- only the vertical rhythm below it shifts. */
+  width: 320px;
+  height: 320px;
 }

